text:
The night is cold, I am restless at home;
A small bird flew past my window last night, singing beautifully;
It chirped "goodnight" as if it were talking to me.
This sound made me feel that nature has not forgotten about people and children.

Thou hast, oh Lord! with gentle hand,
Woven for me a crown of flowers ;
And now ’tis crowned by Thee again
With pearls and gems so rare and showers.

The light that falls upon it glows
Like unto gold or rainbow’s hue;
